course: dictionary
lesson: 14120
title: Microorganisms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A microorganism is a living thing so tiny that you need a microscope to see it. Bacteria, yeast and algae are all microorganisms. Scientists sometimes shorten the word to microbes.
explain: Some microorganisms are useful. «Yeast, a microorganism, makes the bread rise.» Others are harmful and can make you ill. «Germs» is the everyday name for the harmful ones.
explain: Washing your hands helps to remove harmful microorganisms. «Wash your hands before you eat, to remove germs.» Notice how the sentence tells you what to do about them.
fact: A microorganism is a living thing too small to see without a microscope.
fact: Bacteria, yeast and algae are examples of microorganisms.
fact: Microbes is a short name that means the same as microorganisms.
fact: Some microorganisms are useful: they help bread rise and help make yogurt and cheese.
fact: Some microorganisms are harmful: they can make you ill and can make food go off.
exercise: «You can only see the microorganism under a microscope.» What is a microorganism? | A type of rock found in caves | A machine that makes bread | *A living thing so tiny you need a microscope to see it | A large animal that lives in the sea
exercise: «Yeast is a microorganism that helps bread rise.» Is yeast useful or harmful here? | Harmful, because it is a large animal | Neither, because it cannot be alive | Harmful, because it makes you ill | *Useful, because it helps bread rise
exercise: Which word is a short name for microorganisms? | tiger | *microbes | castle | river
test: «Washing your hands removes harmful microorganisms.» What are harmful microorganisms most likely to do? | Make food sweeter | Make you bigger | *Make you ill | Help you see far away
test: Which of these is a microorganism? | *Bacteria | A cup | A rock | A cloud
exam: Mum says, «Some microorganisms in cheese are useful, but others can make food go off.» What does this tell you? | They are all big animals | None of them can be seen | All microorganisms are useful | *Some are useful and some are harmful
